<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A bar of menus for an app's top-level commands.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/menubar)

<%= embed AppicaUI::MenubarPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Menubar(aria_label: "Application") do
  MenubarMenu do
    MenubarTrigger { "File" }
    MenubarContent do
      MenubarItem { "New file" }
      MenubarItem { "Open…" }
      MenubarSub do
        MenubarSubTrigger { "Open recent" }
        MenubarSubContent do
          MenubarItem { "project-alpha" }
          MenubarItem { "landing-page" }
        end
      end
      MenubarSeparator()
      MenubarItem { "Save" }
    end
  end
  MenubarMenu do
    MenubarTrigger { "Edit" }
    MenubarContent do
      MenubarItem { "Undo" }
      MenubarItem { "Redo" }
    end
  end
end
```

The root is the bar that coordinates a row (or column) of menus, sharing `variant:`, `size:` and
`orientation:` with all of them:

- **MenubarMenu** - wraps one menu: a trigger and its popup.
- **MenubarTrigger** - the top-level label that opens its menu. Once any menu is open, moving the pointer
  to a sibling trigger switches to it; arrow keys move focus along the bar.
- **MenubarContent** - the popup for that menu. In a vertical bar it opens to the side.
- **MenubarItem** - one action. Dispatches `appica-ui--menubar:select` and closes the menu by default.
- **MenubarGroup / MenubarGroupLabel / MenubarSeparator** - structure for sectioned menus.
- **MenubarCheckboxItem / MenubarRadioGroup + MenubarRadioItem** - stateful options with a check indicator.
- **MenubarLinkItem** - an item that renders an `<a>` for navigation.
- **MenubarSub / MenubarSubTrigger / MenubarSubContent** - a nested submenu.

Inside an item, put a leading icon on `data: { icon: "start" }`, and push a trailing `Kbd` shortcut to the
edge with `class: "ms-auto"`. All behaviour lives in the `appica-ui--menubar` Stimulus controller.

Reach for a Menubar for the persistent command bar of an application (File / Edit / View …).

## Examples

### Variants

`variant: :pill` (default) gives each trigger a hover/active pill, while `variant: :line` draws an
animated underline - closer to a classic desktop menu bar.

<%= embed AppicaUI::MenubarPreview, :variants %>

### Vertical

`orientation: :vertical` stacks the menus into a sidebar. Triggers can carry a leading icon, and each menu
opens to the inline-end side (below the trigger when there's no room).

<%= embed AppicaUI::MenubarPreview, :vertical %>

```ruby
Menubar(orientation: :vertical, aria_label: "Workspace", class: "w-35") do
  MenubarMenu do
    MenubarTrigger do
      Icon(:folder, data: { icon: "start" })
      plain "Projects"
    end
    MenubarContent { MenubarItem { "All projects" } }
  end
end
```

### Submenus

Nest a `MenubarSub` inside a menu with its own `MenubarSubTrigger` and `MenubarSubContent`. The sub-trigger
shows a chevron and opens to the side on hover, click or the arrow key, flipping near a screen edge.

<%= embed AppicaUI::MenubarPreview, :submenus %>

### Checkbox & radio items

`MenubarCheckboxItem` toggles; a `MenubarRadioGroup` of `MenubarRadioItem`s picks a single value, both
labelled with a `MenubarGroupLabel`. They keep the menu open and dispatch
`appica-ui--menubar:checked-change` ({ item, checked }) and `appica-ui--menubar:value-change` ({ group, value }).

<%= embed AppicaUI::MenubarPreview, :selections %>

```ruby
MenubarContent do
  MenubarGroup do
    MenubarGroupLabel { "Panels" }
    MenubarCheckboxItem(checked: settings.toolbar?) { "Toolbar" }
  end
  MenubarSeparator()
  MenubarRadioGroup(value: settings.theme) do
    MenubarGroupLabel { "Theme" }
    MenubarRadioItem(value: "light") { "Light" }
    MenubarRadioItem(value: "dark") { "Dark" }
  end
end
```

### Leading icons

A leading icon on `data: { icon: "start" }` works on both a `MenubarTrigger` and a `MenubarItem`; pair an
item with a trailing `Kbd` shortcut pushed to the edge with `ms-auto`.

<%= embed AppicaUI::MenubarPreview, :icons %>

```ruby
MenubarItem do
  Icon(:file_plus, data: { icon: "start" })
  plain "New file"
  Kbd(size: :sm, class: "ms-auto") { "⌘N" }
end
```

### Handling selections

Every part is plain markup; listen to the controller's events from your own Stimulus controller:

```ruby
Menubar(aria_label: "Application", data: { action: "appica-ui--menubar:select->editor#command" }) { ... }
```

`event.detail` carries `{ item, label }` - put a `data-command` on the item to tell them apart.

### RTL

The bar lays out from the right, arrow-key focus reverses, and popups and submenus open towards the
inline end.

<%= embed AppicaUI::MenubarPreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Menubar

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:pill`, `:line` | `:pill` | Trigger appearance - hover/active pill, or an animated underline. |
| `size:` | `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg` | `:md` | Scales the triggers, popups, and items together. |
| `orientation:` | `:horizontal`, `:vertical` | `:horizontal` | Lay the bar out as a row or a column. |
| `loop_focus:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Wrap arrow-key focus from the last trigger back to the first. |
| `disabled:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Disable every menu in the bar. |
| `aria_label:`, `class:`, `data:`, … | | | Other attributes go on the bar. |

### MenubarMenu, MenubarTrigger, MenubarContent

| Part | Props |
|------|-------|
| `MenubarMenu` | `disabled:`, `id:` (the trigger and popup ids derive from it) |
| `MenubarTrigger` | `disabled:`, `class:` |
| `MenubarContent` | `class:` on the popup |

### Items

| Part | Props |
|------|-------|
| `MenubarItem` | `disabled:`, `close_on_click:` (default `true`), `label:` (typeahead text) |
| `MenubarLinkItem` | `href:` (required), `close_on_click:`, `label:`, any anchor attribute |
| `MenubarCheckboxItem` | `checked:`, `disabled:`, `close_on_click:` (default `false`), `label:` |
| `MenubarRadioGroup` | `value:` (the selected item's value), `name:` |
| `MenubarRadioItem` | `value:` (required), `disabled:`, `close_on_click:` (default `false`), `label:` |
| `MenubarGroup`, `MenubarGroupLabel`, `MenubarSeparator` | `class:` |
| `MenubarSub`, `MenubarSubTrigger`, `MenubarSubContent` | `disabled:` / `label:` on the sub-trigger; `class:` |

### Events

| Event | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| `appica-ui--menubar:select` | `{ item, label }` |
| `appica-ui--menubar:checked-change` | `{ item, checked }` |
| `appica-ui--menubar:value-change` | `{ group, value }` |
| `appica-ui--menubar:open-change` | `{ menu, open }` |

## Accessibility

- The bar has `role="menubar"`; give it an accessible name with `aria_label:`. Triggers are `menuitem`s
  with `aria-haspopup` and `aria-expanded`, and each popup is a `menu` labelled by its trigger.
- ←/→ (or ↑/↓ when vertical) move focus between triggers (one tab stop for the whole bar); Enter / Space /
  ↓ open a menu; Escape closes it back to its trigger; typeahead jumps to matching items.
- With a menu open, hovering a sibling trigger switches to its menu without an extra click.
- Disabled triggers and items are skipped by keyboard navigation.
- Popup enter/exit transitions are skipped when the user prefers reduced motion.
